# Gradle's own bookkeeping, the wrapper, and one machine's SDK location.
#
# Unlike Flutter's template, this file does **not** ignore the Gradle wrapper. This
# repository has to provide `./gradlew`, `gradlew.bat` and
# `gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar` — all three are committed here, and
# `dart tool/verify_release.dart` fails if a .gitignore in this tree excludes one of
# them, because `git add -A` would then leave it out of the repository and the
# documented build entry point would not work in a fresh clone. (Flutter hides the
# omission by injecting its own copies at build time.)
/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Keystores.
#
# **This repository must never contain one.** `keystore.properties`, `*.jks`,
# `*.keystore`, `*.p12`, `*.pem` and `*.pk8` all stay ignored, and
# `dart tool/verify_release.dart` fails on any of them, on a `storePassword=` line and
# on a negation of these patterns.
#
# The maintainer's own key is *not* here: it is tracked on purpose in the private
# development repository, where git history is the backup, and it is dropped by name
# during the export. A key that can impersonate this app cannot be un-published, so
# the only safe answer for a public repository is that it was never there.
#
# See RELEASING.md for the keytool invocation, the validity to choose and the
# procedure. To make a local build without the key, use
# `flutter build apk --release --android-project-arg=allowDebugSigning=true`, which is
# debug-signed on purpose and refuses to pass the artifact check unless you say so.
key.properties
keystore.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/*.p12
**/*.pem
**/*.pk8
